  "discussion_thread_url": "https://sourceforge.net/rest/p/apc-aa/feature-requests/_discuss/thread/cd992aec/",
  "created_date": "2002-11-08 18:24:42",
  "ticket_num": 16,
  "summary": "FrmInputMultiChBox - wrapping fix",
  "description": "When using multiple checkboxes to show an array of \nconstants on an itemedit form ... line wrapping is not \nalways elegant. \r\n\r\nWe always want the check box \nand the full label to appear on one line:\r\n\r\n\\[ \\] label here  \\[ \\] \nlabel here  \r\n\\[ \\] label here  \\[ \\] label here \r\n\r\nWith many \nconstants defined, the wrap can happen after the \ncheckbox, or between the label words: \r\n\r\n\\[ \\] label here  \n\\[ \\] label here  \\[ \\] label \r\nhere  \\[ \\] label here \r\n\r\nSimple \nsolution is to add NOBR tags around each whole unit. \nEdited function attached.\r\n\r\nAre there browser \ncompatibility issues with using NOBRs in this way? \\(I've \nbeen using this edited function for months -- no probs.\\)",
  "reported_by": "jhall",
  "assigned_to": null,
  "reported_by_id": "519a55f034309d2f05e44557",
