  "discussion_thread_url": "https://sourceforge.net/rest/p/apc-aa/feature-requests/_discuss/thread/1589c004/",
  "created_date": "2002-12-17 18:57:53",
  "ticket_num": 18,
  "summary": "End user permissions module",
  "description": "There is currently a need for an end user permissions \r\nmodule. This module would provide the following:\r\n\r\n\\- Authentication for native AA end user systems like \r\nAlerts \r\n\\- Authentication for end user modules plugged in using \r\nmodule system\r\n\\- Ability to use as authentication method for other PHP \r\napps on the same server\r\n\\- Ability to use as simple directory level HTTP \r\nauthentication for HTML pages that wrap around and \r\nActionApps site\r\n\\- Single user profile for each user that is tied into all of \r\nthese applications\r\n\\- Ability to add custom fields to the user profile\r\n\\- Ability to track information that users have accessed \r\nfrom AA and Alerts \\(future\\)\r\n\\- Record level authentication \\(e.g. for reading individual \r\nAA articles\\) \\(future\\)\r\n\r\nSome of the work for this is already underway for the \r\nAlerts system. However, new demands that are beyond \r\nwhat we are doing for Alerts could emerge quickly \\(see \r\nlist above\\). \r\n\r\nSponosorhship: Depending on cost, these features \r\ncould be sponsored by the CEH and PKRN projects \r\ncurrently managed by Commons Group\r\n",
  "reported_by": "msurman",
  "assigned_to": null,
